WEBVTT

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:50.520
Wow, this is surprising. Since when did
that lady become such a good R driver?

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.880
She has a lot more power than me.

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:59.920
<i>Monster Machine</i>

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:05.630
<i>He's behind me.</i>

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:09.640
<i>Even now it feels like it'll go one forever.</i>

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:17.580
<i>A moment more understandable that one million words.</i>

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:26.360
<i>Right now, with this car behind me. This feeling of unity.</i>

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:55.060
<i>Listen Reina-chan, don't misunderstand.
You aren't to race ahead of that Z.</i>

00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:00.040
<i>I just want you to catch up.</i>

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.290
Geez, you've turned into one crazy girl, haven't you?

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:19.610
Huh?

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:24.800
You drove this R like that based on feeling alone. Well done.

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:32.300
But from another viewpoint, I'd say the
narrow twisty circuit only let you go so far.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.000
Mostly, second or third gear.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.040
Sometimes you'd hit fourth but only for a second.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:43.570
You haven't been able to use the last of the 800hp, right?

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:45.970
Scary, isn't it?

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:47.570
Very scary.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:51.580
That's good. Don't forget the fear, now.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:55.830
I get it but... don't get it either.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.970
This old man says crazy things.

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:09.680
It means you have your R. Yamamoto's R
is like that. Don't forget that feeling.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:15.480
On the other hand, forget about this GT-R today.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:26.240
It's a good sound for the RB26, don't you think?

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.450
It's fast and...

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.160
I was really racing.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:33.700
I know.

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:41.630
Takagi!

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:50.300
Hey, hey! There's only BMW's and Mercedes here!

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.890
It has to be like this for the big money, eh?

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:56.390
No, no. There's some domestics around, too.

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:57.880
Like what?

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.260
Where's the BlackBird?

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:02.910
It's done. It went to Kitami-san's warehouse, three days ago.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.460
There's still the engine to put in.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.380
Did you patch up, right?

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:12.820
It's not about that. It's just that there wasn't enough time.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:15.330
All that's left is to try it out, huh?

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:20.330
An 800hp FR. That and a body that can't keep up.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:34.720
Alright then, I'll give it a try.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:47.690
<i>As expected from the genius bodywork of Takagi and Kitami Jun.</i>

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:58.660
<i>It's perfect. It's become the ideal Porsche 911 Turbo.</i>

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.660
This is worse than I thought.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:07.970
The so called "stance" is warped. I'm surprise he raced like this.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:10.940
From the outside it doesn't look like it huh?

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:13.380
What happened to the original rigidity of the Supra?

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:18.630
That's alright. It'll just be like a new car's now, though.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:22.480
Normally, it would be three years, 30,000km.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:24.100
This sound...

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.190
It's an L6.

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:27.700
It's the Z.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.670
You just got back?

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:33.840
Yeah. I was just out racing.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:34.990
Some lights were on me.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:39.500
Perfect timing. I was just thinking that I wanted to see you.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.140
Come on in, there's something I want to show you.

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:51.050
I'll introduce you. These guys used to
be at the top with Kitami-san back then,

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:55.710
RGO's Ohta-san and Yamamoto Speed's Yamamoto-san.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:56.590
Nice to meet you.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.220
I'm Asakura Akio, pleased to meet you.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:03.720
<i>This boy is the Devil Z's driver...</i>

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:08.210
Akio, you know this Supra, right?

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:08.730
Yeah.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:12.480
Akio, I've got a favor to ask.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:13.430
Favor?

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.870
Will you help me with this?

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:18.980
This Supra needs work.

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:19.630
Me?

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:23.990
Once it's done, it'll become an 800hp monster FR.

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:28.630
It'll be in front of you for sure. Even still, I'd like your help.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:33.670
I understand, let me try.

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:35.390
No... I want to try.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:38.740
You can come after you're done with work.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:40.360
I'll pay you as well.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:41.980
No, you don't need to...

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:42.980
No!

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:46.990
I didn't ask for a volunteer,

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:48.610
you'll accept the pay, alright?

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:50.510
Then, you'll really work.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:56.000
I didn't take any money for your Z or the BlackBird.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:59.410
That means I don't take any responsibility.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:03.660
I was just pursuing the ideal, no...
just looking to make the ideal body and chassis.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:06.370
It's not strange if something happened some time.

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:10.130
You guys still move forward.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.090
I don't expect something like that.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.090
You're special.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:22.100
And this Supra is different. The person driving it is special to us.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:30.600
Hey, beer!

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:34.970
Oh, Rikako-chan! You've become prettier!

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:40.090
Ah, quit it! We're a group of geezers, we can't talk to them now.

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:44.240
That's not true, right? She's just Ohta's daughter.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:47.710
Huh? Where'd those two go anyway?

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:52.250
We haven't changed at all, huh?

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.400
Yeah.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:58.960
We all look different but we're still the same inside, huh?

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:02.680
Anyway, the chassis is in Takagi's hands.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:07.260
Alright! Next is the muffler! Right?!

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:10.070
Gacchan, when did you become the leader?
<i>Gacchan - Sasaki Gen's nickname</i>

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:17.520
Hey, who are we really doing this for?

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:20.620
For ourselves, of course.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:25.830
Not for Aizawa nor his son.

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:31.340
We're creating a machine to beat the Devil Z for our own sake.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:35.890
That's true. It's all for ourselves, huh?

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:40.220
Creating the car, plus trying to hit the limits.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:45.570
Either way, that's how our lives are.

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:50.070
When I was just starting on body work,

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:54.320
a lot of tuners were neglecting the body.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:57.580
To everyone, the engine is life.

00:09:57.580 --> 00:10:02.980
If the body was bad, they'd find another one to put the engine in.

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:05.640
I've seen so many cars like that.

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:12.990
Since I work with the body, I didn't
like how tuners overused the bodies.

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:19.050
But I've tried a lot of things and always found it futile.

00:10:19.750 --> 00:10:21.550
Body reinforcement isn't magic.

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:25.560
No matter how much support you build.

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:29.050
It doesn't matter if you squeeze so much into it.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:43.960
In preparation for that, I intend to fix up the rear.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:48.560
To be able to take 800hp and hold it while driving,

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:51.750
you need to sacrifice some of the body for some flexibility.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.540
All to beat your Z.

00:10:56.010 --> 00:11:02.710
I'm just joking. I like you and your Z.

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:06.180
On the other side, I don't want it to be the only one.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:15.400
I'm sure Kitami-san, BlackBird, Yamamoto-san and
the others have taken an interest in you and your Z.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:19.940
Holding their breaths, working to reach the very top of the limit.

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:39.320
You're late! We've been waiting forever for you to come.

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:41.970
Good work, kid.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:43.980
Ah, thanks.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:46.190
It took a little longer than expected, huh?

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:47.390
I'm sorry.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:49.960
But, I'm feeling good about it, though.

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:52.030
Please give it an extraordinary engine.

00:11:52.030 --> 00:11:54.340
Yeah, that's done.

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:55.590
And suspension?

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:57.020
Of course, Ueda's got it.

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:00.020
The loudest one from back then.

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:04.430
Yoshio's taking care of the exhaust. We can trust his work.

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:07.460
Lastly, Tominaga is taking care of the ECU settings.

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:13.730
Amazing! It looks like it'll be a top-notch job with this group.

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:15.610
Then, it's my intake!

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:17.880
Yeah. Put in a powerful duct.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:23.560
Make it like the original you made for the Z31 back then.

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:25.000
I know that!

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:27.930
I don't need a crybaby like you to tell me!

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:32.800
You're still interested in the rear?

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:33.680
Is it ok?

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:40.700
Well, give it a try. If Takagi says the body is ok, there's no worries.

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:44.430
Good night. Please be careful.

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:50.700
Hello, Kei speaking.

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:54.070
Is that so? Only a couple more days...

00:12:54.070 --> 00:12:59.010
Yeah, definitely. Get ready and wait for it.

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:01.120
It's one hell of a monster Supra.

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:02.710
I look forward to it.

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:08.900
<i>Though it cost a lot, the tires are brand new.</i>

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:13.250
<i>Gears, engine oil and everything is being replaced.</i>

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:15.990
<i>Kei will get it in a week.</i>

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:19.020
<i>You can wait for the race next week.</i>

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:22.540
<i>Even the Devil Z could be in trouble this time.</i>

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:25.320
<i>Everything favors the Supra.</i>

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:27.740
<i>You should know that best.</i>

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:32.010
<i>Before a legendary machine turns into a normal car,</i>

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:35.990
<i>you'll be given the choice, Akio.</i>

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.630
Oh? Here he comes.

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:50.570
This way, Kei.

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:58.830
We've left you waiting. Take it.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:14.010
<i>It's completely different...</i>

00:14:14.010 --> 00:14:15.920
One week.

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:18.690
If you can't master it in one week,

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:23.000
you won't be able to drive this 800hp Supra ever again.

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:37.640
<i>First, match its wavelength.</i>

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:40.970
<i>And then sense...</i>

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:44.110
<i>This isn't something you can find a solution to in time.</i>

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:47.020
<i>If you can't do it, forget about Z.</i>

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:53.110
<i>Those are the conditions to hand over the car.</i>

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:11.820
<i>Everything favors the Supra.</i>

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:15.800
<i>Before a legendary machine turns into a normal car,</i>

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:18.820
<i>you'll be given the choice.</i>

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:30.570
Long time no see.

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:31.450
Kei...

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.980
Looks like this Supra packs a punch.

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:38.280
I hear it's pretty fast.

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:39.200
Which turbo?

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:41.100
A TD06 Twin Turbo.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:43.990
Oh? You've gone somewhere cool.

00:15:43.990 --> 00:15:47.050
Kohta, where's your S14?

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:47.060
Eh, I sold it.
Kohta, where's your S14?

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:48.920
Eh, I sold it.

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:50.460
Sold it?

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:52.000
Kei...

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:55.470
Have you thought about your future at all?

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:57.360
You'll end up repeating university like this.

00:15:57.360 --> 00:15:59.100
You can't stay a host forever.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:02.020
That's alright...

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:03.550
Give me a real answer.

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:08.370
Once we've graduated, Maki and I are getting married.

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:12.230
Is that so? I'm happy for you guys.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:17.470
It's true cars were fun. Everyone was so into it.

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:19.860
But it's over now.

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:26.180
Kei, do you remember what the
seniors told us when we first started?

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:27.980
Short run, 2 years.

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:29.420
Long run, 4 years.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:33.490
That's right. Either or short run of
two years or a long run of four years.

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:38.430
Tuning cars, racing and all the other irresponsible things.

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:41.770
We've done two years.

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:44.240
Everyone but you already stopped.

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:46.520
You're by yourself now.

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:49.320
I'm by myself?

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:53.320
No, I've got friends now, too.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:56.730
Kei, wait.

00:16:56.730 --> 00:16:59.050
I'm not alone.

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:01.010
You're with those friends today?

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:01.910
Yeah.

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:07.450
See ya.

00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:20.690
Maki... you, me and all of our friends...
he's not looking at us anymore.

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:26.020
Would you like another coffee?

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.180
No, thank you. I'm leaving now.

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:29.830
Right now?

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:33.060
Yes. I think I'll be seeing some friends.

00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:35.490
I was thinking that earlier.

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:39.820
Is it for some special reason?

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:41.680
Some reason or another.

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:45.450
It's not like I knew it.

00:17:45.450 --> 00:17:47.290
I feel like they're calling me.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:50.540
Were they people that have come here before?

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:53.540
Yes, they have but...

00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:56.670
I don't know when but I stopped hearing his voice.

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:59.170
I she in another world now?

00:17:59.630 --> 00:18:00.280
Yes.

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:06.350
A now it seems like I've started
to hear some new friend's voices.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.970
<i>As time moves on, friends come and go.</i>

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:20.020
<i>But as you race, you'll definitely begin to hear new voices.</i>

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:27.830
<i>BlackBird!</i>

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:35.830
<i>We're no match for that Supra.</i>

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:41.010
<i>But we can't just leave it at that, Z.</i>

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:47.130
Yes?

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:48.530
It's Shima.

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:52.850
I just saw the Supra on the outer ring
of the Tokai-Kanjo expressway.

00:18:52.850 --> 00:18:53.980
Is that so?

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:56.860
I don't want you to wait and see the result,

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:59.980
so I was thinking I'd pick you up, Kitami-san.

00:18:59.980 --> 00:19:04.000
You'd like me to sit and watch from up front?

00:19:05.690 --> 00:19:07.080
Alright then.

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:12.510
Aizawa...

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:14.240
<i>Hey, Kitami-san,</i>

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:16.790
<i>what do you think we'll be doing in 15 years?</i>

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:20.330
<i>How would I know something like that?</i>

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:24.050
<i>In 15 years, my kid will be driving, you know!</i>

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:26.530
<i>It seems unbelievable.</i>

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:30.530
<i>But that kid doesn't seem to like cars that much.</i>

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:33.230
<i>He's just hanging out with girls at the nursery.</i>

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:35.890
<i>Nah, he's your son, isn't he?</i>

00:19:35.890 --> 00:19:37.460
<i>Once he hits middle school,</i>

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:39.060
<i>he'll be driving motorcycles with no license.</i>

00:19:39.060 --> 00:19:43.440
<i>Sounds like it. From there it's cars, huh?</i>

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:49.120
<i>I'm always thinking about how to make my car faster.</i>

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:53.020
<i>It's obvious I've become addicted.</i>

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:55.860
<i>Kitami-san...</i>

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:58.010
<i>I wonder if you can tell me...</i>

00:19:58.010 --> 00:19:58.840
<i>About what?</i>

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:02.730
<i>If Kei will end up like me in 15 years,</i>

00:20:02.730 --> 00:20:05.840
<i>tuning cars and all that foolish stuff.</i>

00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:07.990
<i>You tell me.</i>

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:09.850
<i>I can't...</i>

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:12.970
<i>Because I've become someone who knows the foolishness,</i>

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:15.230
<i>yet can't stop.</i>

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:23.730
It's been 15 years.

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:29.640
Now your son is driving, too.

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:39.000
<i>I knew it, it's tonight...</i>

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:44.980
<i>The Z, Supra and BlackBird...</i>

00:20:44.980 --> 00:20:48.000
<i>The ultimate rivalry between the three monster machines.</i>

00:21:04.010 --> 00:21:06.090
Where's the Supra?

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:08.340
I was with him until I left the expressway.

00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:10.860
He's most likely still on there.

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:15.320
Do you know the Supra driver?

00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:18.910
Yeah. He's the son of an old friend.

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:21.540
At least, I know the name.

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:26.920
He's the only son of the late "ultimate demon runner", Aizawa Koichi.

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:31.050
I know that. Is it alright for me to drive seriously?

00:21:31.050 --> 00:21:34.400
Of course, go all out.

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:38.570
My bonds with people don't matter in your race.

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:50.820
He's here, Kitami-san. It's the Supra.

00:22:09.770 --> 00:22:12.470
<i>There they are. BlackBird and Kei's Supra!</i>

00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:20.770
<i>So, it's started...</i>

00:23:04.310 --> 00:23:07.020
<i>The BlackBird in front...</i>

00:23:07.030 --> 00:23:08.120
<i>and the Z behind me.</i>
